WEBVTT

00:53.011 --> 00:56.014
What's taking the manager so long?

00:56.014 --> 00:57.124
Here I am!

00:57.766 --> 00:58.850
Hello!

00:58.850 --> 01:02.187
I'm Arale Nakamachi, soon joining
Kanda Shiroyama Academy!

01:02.187 --> 01:06.066
Thank you for inviting me
to this creators' gathering.

01:06.066 --> 01:08.986
I'm really honored to be here today.

01:08.986 --> 01:12.030
I might be a bit troublesome at times,

01:12.030 --> 01:14.909
but I really hope we can get along!

01:14.909 --> 01:17.452
- She glitched?
- Relax, Nakamachi-san.

01:17.452 --> 01:19.538
Take a deep breath.

01:19.538 --> 01:21.790
Yes, let's take a deep breath.

01:26.104 --> 01:27.170
Why, though?

01:27.170 --> 01:30.048
Oh, nice! That's totally MewType!

01:30.048 --> 01:31.717
- "Mew"?
- What's that?

01:31.717 --> 01:34.512
My bad. I should've started with this.

01:34.512 --> 01:38.098
Starting today, you're called MewType!

01:38.974 --> 01:40.992
"MewType"?

01:40.992 --> 01:42.603
A new creature?

01:42.603 --> 01:45.313
It's your group name, obviously!

01:45.313 --> 01:46.565
A gro...

01:48.026 --> 01:49.277
Arale Nakamachi.

01:49.277 --> 01:50.777
Nonoka Miyanaga.

01:50.777 --> 01:52.155
Yuno Sengoku.

01:52.155 --> 01:53.280
Miyako Fuji.

01:53.280 --> 01:55.282
Huh?! M... me too?

01:55.282 --> 01:59.328
That's right!
All of you together are MewType!

02:00.287 --> 02:01.913
I'm so excited.

02:01.913 --> 02:05.834
- That's news to me.
- You said I'd only do illustrations.

02:05.834 --> 02:08.502
No way. It's written in your contract.

02:08.502 --> 02:09.254
(Member of a band or group)

02:09.254 --> 02:10.797
(Member of a band or group)
I don't remember.

02:10.797 --> 02:14.468
I remember drawing a red line
while explaining it.

02:14.468 --> 02:15.592
For you too.

02:16.428 --> 02:19.139
I was running on no sleep at the time...

02:19.139 --> 02:20.891
This is a serious matter!

02:20.891 --> 02:25.895
Uh... I don't think being
in a group is for me...

02:26.563 --> 02:29.733
No, I can't! I'm getting flashbacks!

02:29.733 --> 02:33.362
Oh, don't worry. This isn't a group.

02:33.362 --> 02:36.406
It's a band. See? No worries.

02:36.406 --> 02:39.576
Oh, all right. If it's a band, then...

02:39.576 --> 02:42.954
Huh?! That's not it!

02:42.954 --> 02:45.707
Yes, so it's not a group, right?

02:45.707 --> 02:47.292
It's the same thing.

02:47.292 --> 02:50.169
We'll still be working as a group.

02:50.169 --> 02:51.546
I agree with her.

02:52.172 --> 02:54.341
I'm done with bands.

02:54.341 --> 02:57.344
There are enough of them
out there already.

02:58.566 --> 02:59.609
Creepy.

02:59.609 --> 03:03.183
Come on... You really don't get
your own worth, do you?

03:03.183 --> 03:05.977
There's no way we'd lose
with these members.

03:06.603 --> 03:10.482
Everyone except Fuji-san
has an audience on their channel.

03:10.482 --> 03:12.901
Miyanaga-san's cover
even hit 100 million views.

03:12.901 --> 03:13.985
How many?!

03:15.862 --> 03:20.325
"I'm chasing rabbits..."

03:20.867 --> 03:23.729
Oh wow, it's Usa Eater-chan!

03:23.729 --> 03:27.374
- Is this you? - I was five!
- Seven, eight zeros... 100 million views?

03:28.750 --> 03:32.254
You're the Usa Eater-chan
that all of humanity has seen!!

03:32.254 --> 03:36.258
I can't believe I'm actually meeting
a real internet celebrity!

03:36.800 --> 03:39.302
Arale-chan, you post videos too, right?

03:41.430 --> 03:45.308
I heard that cover you posted recently.

03:45.308 --> 03:50.564
You looked so happy
singing in that video...

03:50.564 --> 03:52.191
I love it.

03:52.191 --> 03:53.594
Y... you do?

03:53.594 --> 03:55.569
Yeah. I love it!

03:57.154 --> 04:02.367
My singing is really nothing special...

04:02.367 --> 04:06.413
I've been told my voice
is pretty loud in class, but...

04:06.413 --> 04:10.859
"Love"? That's saying too much.
I'm not that special...

04:11.501 --> 04:14.254
So... Do you really like it?

04:14.254 --> 04:19.134
Yeah! I absolutely love your singing!

04:22.303 --> 04:26.933
We're better off using our strengths
than forming a band now.

04:26.933 --> 04:29.422
I've got branding to consider.

04:29.422 --> 04:30.437
Excuse me.

04:30.437 --> 04:33.648
I can't just start a band...

04:33.648 --> 04:35.442
Oh, don't worry.

04:36.651 --> 04:38.820
I made enough time to practice!

04:38.820 --> 04:42.407
Joint practice is on this schedule.
Make sure to practice on your own too.

04:42.407 --> 04:44.242
- Make sure to practice on your own too.
- I'm playing the guitar!

04:44.242 --> 04:47.162
- While you keep posting on your channels,
- I'm playing the guitar!

04:47.162 --> 04:50.243
we'll practice hard
before putting on a live show.

04:50.243 --> 04:51.291
A live show?!

04:51.291 --> 04:55.962
We want at least one original song,
so let's work on songwriting.

04:55.962 --> 04:59.841
Sengoku-san can do the music
and Nakamachi-san, the lyrics.

05:02.219 --> 05:04.471
Let's try to give it our best!

05:04.471 --> 05:06.515
Yay!

05:08.725 --> 05:10.351
(You are offline)

05:14.064 --> 05:16.440
(Are dreams really power?)

05:18.818 --> 05:22.198
No way I can handle
a band or a live show!

05:22.198 --> 05:26.827
I can't stand in front of people,
let alone show my face!

05:26.827 --> 05:30.121
I thought I was only going to sing...

05:32.457 --> 05:36.419
Tomorrow's my first day of high school,
but I feel so tense.

05:43.589 --> 05:44.761
If I don't sing,

05:44.761 --> 05:47.389
(I might be a bit troublesome at times...)
I won't have to join a band!

05:47.389 --> 05:50.600
Then I can skip the shows
and hide my face!

05:50.600 --> 05:52.269
I might be a genius!

05:53.270 --> 05:55.522
I won't sing for a while!

06:03.988 --> 06:08.577
ready set and find out ready set and find out
it's only one newtype

06:09.494 --> 06:14.207
The story always revolves around us

06:14.207 --> 06:19.296
That may be a given, but let me repeat it

06:19.296 --> 06:24.342
Can you read the guidelines?
No matter how carefully we write them

06:24.551 --> 06:29.472
Why does something always get in the way?
Still, we'll make it roar!

06:29.472 --> 06:33.476
In a heartbeat, like an overdrive

06:33.476 --> 06:40.275
We yearn to distort the world we see

06:40.275 --> 06:44.904
Seeing too clearly makes innocence
seem ridiculous, what a joke!

06:45.113 --> 06:50.035
Even vain attempts at being brave
Will be rewarded when the time comes

06:50.035 --> 06:53.872
This is the plot of our survival

06:53.872 --> 06:59.628
Rewriting the tale
Shedding absurd tears, the newtype way

06:59.628 --> 07:04.299
We can go anywhere, we can, so don't stop now

07:04.299 --> 07:08.887
Not an anime, not real either,
let's make our own category

07:08.887 --> 07:12.057
We've grown tired
of this complicated, dull world!

07:12.057 --> 07:15.393
Leave it to us, we'll write our own dreams

07:15.602 --> 07:18.939
ready set and find out ready set and find out
it's only one newtype, our choice

07:18.939 --> 07:20.565
Following the steady beat

07:20.565 --> 07:25.487
ready set and find out ready set and find out
it's only one newtype

07:56.393 --> 07:57.996
Shut up.

07:57.996 --> 08:00.146
All you talk about is yourself.

08:00.146 --> 08:01.398
Are you listening?

08:01.398 --> 08:03.692
- Selfish.
- You asked for it.

08:03.692 --> 08:06.361
- You hurt people.
- Are you running away?

08:06.361 --> 08:08.279
Good luck in your next life.

08:10.115 --> 08:16.204
"Dreams are power!"

08:16.204 --> 08:21.418
"Dreams are power!"

08:24.254 --> 08:29.300
Here at Kanda Shiroyama Academy,
we honor our students' wishes above all.

08:29.300 --> 08:34.054
We hope you will never lose sight
of what you truly want to do.

08:34.946 --> 08:36.307
Oh, it's Magilulu!

08:37.058 --> 08:38.559
From the last movie.

08:38.559 --> 08:40.562
What? They made stickers?

08:42.154 --> 08:44.482
Yeah, I like Magilulu.

08:45.175 --> 08:46.568
You have good taste!

08:46.568 --> 08:48.820
It sold out so quickly!

08:48.820 --> 08:51.155
It was a limited-edition sticker!

08:51.155 --> 08:54.367
My family split up
across Tokyo to look for them.

08:54.367 --> 08:56.828
We managed to get two stickers!

08:59.747 --> 09:01.624
Our station's that way.

09:01.624 --> 09:03.083
I take the subway.

09:03.083 --> 09:05.378
- Okay, then.
- Bye.

09:05.378 --> 09:07.589
- Bye!
- See you tomorrow.

09:11.843 --> 09:14.054
Magilulu fans are a blessing!

09:14.054 --> 09:18.600
Judging by today, I might actually
survive going to school in person.

09:19.851 --> 09:21.727
(5 PM: MewType practice)

09:22.937 --> 09:26.399
As I said before,
we'll start with your videos.

09:26.399 --> 09:29.360
Any songs you'd like to cover,
Nakamachi-san?

09:29.360 --> 09:31.237
The Magilulu opening song!

09:31.237 --> 09:32.780
- I'm not singing!
- Nice!

09:32.780 --> 09:36.034
I'll play "I love Nana-chan song"!

09:36.034 --> 09:40.121
- Who's that?
- Nanaka-chan! My baby sister!

09:40.121 --> 09:45.668
Right. Next is Fuji-san... but you have
another job to prioritize this month.

09:45.668 --> 09:48.546
Sengoku-san is focusing
on writing music too.

09:48.546 --> 09:49.465
For now.

09:49.465 --> 09:52.550
So it's just us two. Pretty lonely, huh?

09:52.550 --> 09:54.344
Well, I guess...

09:54.344 --> 09:57.013
After your solo videos,
you'll do a collab.

09:57.013 --> 10:00.892
Yay! Sounds great!
A Yuno-chan song collab!

10:00.892 --> 10:03.102
Are you serious, Miyanaga-san?!

10:03.102 --> 10:06.606
I have a deadline coming up.
I'm not composing.

10:06.606 --> 10:09.651
I... I might not be able to sing either.

10:10.151 --> 10:11.736
Oh no, you can't?

10:11.736 --> 10:14.322
How good are you with instruments?

10:14.322 --> 10:17.951
Let's see... If it's new to me,
I'll need to practice a lot.

10:17.951 --> 10:23.414
About our next practice,
I have a manuscript due, so...

10:23.877 --> 10:26.208
"A manuscript"?!

10:26.208 --> 10:28.294
Fuji-san has her manga series.

10:28.294 --> 10:30.255
Wow! What's it called?

10:30.255 --> 10:31.923
I'm still pretty new.

10:31.923 --> 10:33.867
I might know your pen name.

10:35.135 --> 10:37.386
(Chupacabu Saturation
Yako Fujimi) Here.

10:39.681 --> 10:41.725
- You're Yako Fujimi-sensei.
- Yes.

10:41.725 --> 10:45.102
You used to draw fan art
of "Magical Physical Kululu."

10:45.436 --> 10:50.024
I've been following your work
since I was in sixth grade.

10:50.024 --> 10:53.361
Fuji-san handles the artwork
for MewType as well.

10:53.361 --> 10:56.030
What?! N... no way! Let me see!

10:56.030 --> 10:59.450
Here you go. A freshly made account.

10:59.450 --> 11:02.996
I want to keep updating it,
so let's head to practice.

11:02.996 --> 11:04.747
Yay!

11:04.747 --> 11:06.166
Let's switch floors.

11:15.508 --> 11:16.719
A microphone!

11:16.719 --> 11:18.178
I'm not singing.

11:24.666 --> 11:26.852
Connection's good!

11:26.852 --> 11:30.840
Sengoku-san has a lot of tracks
we can use for practice.

11:31.611 --> 11:32.679
You do, right?

11:33.222 --> 11:34.498
Hold on.

11:43.285 --> 11:45.914
It's just the instrumental.

11:45.914 --> 11:48.124
I won't have to sing.

11:51.211 --> 11:53.213
This is tricky.

11:53.213 --> 11:55.881
- Here's the score.
- Oh, thanks!

12:05.934 --> 12:08.311
I'll get the hang of it eventually.

12:15.193 --> 12:17.528
Oh, this is Yuno-chan's song!

12:18.238 --> 12:20.657
She made this song!

12:21.532 --> 12:22.784
How did you know?

12:22.784 --> 12:27.997
Nana-chan asked me to play
your band's songs before,

12:27.997 --> 12:31.107
and I practiced them
over and over again.

12:31.107 --> 12:36.841
Your songs make everyone happy,
so I play them often.

12:38.466 --> 12:39.467
I see.

12:43.389 --> 12:45.665
Huh? Why's the atmosphere so heavy?

12:46.224 --> 12:50.687
All right! You're way too formal.
Why don't we use nicknames?

12:50.687 --> 12:52.647
Great idea!

12:52.647 --> 12:54.440
Arale-chan, you can be...

12:54.440 --> 12:57.318
Ara... Ale... le...

12:57.318 --> 12:59.654
You don't need to worry about me!

12:59.654 --> 13:02.407
Then, I'll be Nono-chan!

13:02.407 --> 13:03.325
Okay...

13:03.325 --> 13:05.535
- Ready?
- What?!

13:05.535 --> 13:10.081
No... Nono... No...

13:10.081 --> 13:15.962
Nono... Nono... Nonono...

13:20.192 --> 13:21.217
Huh?

13:21.217 --> 13:23.344
Arale-chan!

13:25.054 --> 13:26.097
What?

13:28.224 --> 13:30.684
At least you're not bleeding.

13:30.684 --> 13:31.602
Hm...

13:31.602 --> 13:33.980
Now, let's start practicing!

13:33.980 --> 13:35.273
Okay!

13:35.273 --> 13:38.568
Nakamachi-san, just watch
and give your tongue a rest.

13:38.568 --> 13:40.111
Yesh...

13:54.333 --> 13:58.129
I'll practice and get a bit better
by the next session.

13:58.129 --> 14:00.631
- How'd I do?
- Average.

14:00.631 --> 14:02.383
She complimented me!

14:02.383 --> 14:03.968
I didn't.

14:03.968 --> 14:08.264
I'm glad I don't have to sing,
but I'm kind of bored...

14:08.986 --> 14:11.517
I wonder what band Sengoku-san was in.

14:12.268 --> 14:14.395
"Yuno Sengoku..."

14:15.104 --> 14:17.273
They split up two years ago.

14:18.149 --> 14:21.669
Whoa... she wrote so many songs.

14:22.486 --> 14:24.655
She even did the song
for "Nobishimo-den"!

14:24.655 --> 14:27.700
I remember this legendary free game!

14:27.700 --> 14:31.829
The first ones were silly,
but this one had a dark story.

14:31.829 --> 14:35.041
I cried through it
with my friends in sixth grade.

14:37.126 --> 14:40.296
Does this song... sound similar?

14:41.089 --> 14:42.924
We should play "Kamome no yoru" too!

14:43.800 --> 14:48.346
It's what later became
the theme song of "Hijiyori-den," right?

14:48.346 --> 14:51.974
That's the second game
in the tragic trilogy!

14:51.974 --> 14:54.644
It's linked to the first song,
"Kamome no yoru!"

14:54.644 --> 14:58.523
It won't make sense
if we don't start with this song!

14:59.816 --> 15:01.025
What are you saying?

15:10.451 --> 15:14.789
Today, my life was a total disaster...

15:14.789 --> 15:17.208
I messed up again!

15:17.208 --> 15:21.879
I got way too excited, started babbling,
and almost tried to sing.

15:23.089 --> 15:25.609
Things went well at school,
so I got carried away

15:25.609 --> 15:28.177
and troubled Yuno-san-chan-san!

15:28.177 --> 15:29.679
I messed up!

15:30.265 --> 15:32.309
I'm a total disaster...

15:35.716 --> 15:38.879
I wonder if I can be
a small disaster tomorrow.

15:39.480 --> 15:42.859
Tomorrow's rules!
One, no careless talk!

15:42.859 --> 15:44.610
Two, no singing!

15:44.610 --> 15:47.196
Three, no talking or singing at all!

15:48.106 --> 15:49.441
Goodnight!

15:56.025 --> 16:00.693
I'm doing my best at school,
so maybe I'll be fine in the end.

16:03.045 --> 16:04.338
Oh?

16:04.338 --> 16:07.258
Ritsu, look!

16:15.516 --> 16:17.226
Arale-chan.

16:17.810 --> 16:19.687
Long time no see.

16:21.189 --> 16:22.799
How have you been?

16:23.448 --> 16:27.012
You two haven't seen each other
in a while, right?

16:28.613 --> 16:33.451
Clematis? You were in the same group,
so you could at least say something.

16:35.995 --> 16:38.080
You changed your hair.

16:38.080 --> 16:42.668
What a shame.
You were adorable in pigtails.

16:43.377 --> 16:46.130
Is it because you joined a new group?

16:47.006 --> 16:48.633
How did you...

16:48.633 --> 16:53.763
How could I not know
my beloved Arale-chan's latest news?

16:53.763 --> 16:58.392
Oh, right! We formed a new group too!

16:58.392 --> 17:01.771
We're holding our first
in-person event soon.

17:01.771 --> 17:04.232
I wish you could come too.

17:05.273 --> 17:11.446
But if your old fans see you,
things could get messy...

17:11.446 --> 17:13.157
Oh, Arale-chan!

17:13.157 --> 17:15.910
We're here. Are these your friends?

17:15.910 --> 17:16.953
Hello.

17:16.953 --> 17:18.537
- Hello.
- Hi.

17:18.537 --> 17:20.830
Are you Arale-chan's friends?

17:20.830 --> 17:22.917
- Yes!
- We go to the same school.

17:24.167 --> 17:25.920
Arale-chan?

17:25.920 --> 17:27.213
Wait!

17:27.213 --> 17:28.652
Arale-chan!

17:43.020 --> 17:44.564
She switched schools.

17:45.231 --> 17:51.195
She passed that tough middle school exam
and was supposed to go on to university.

17:52.297 --> 17:54.724
Maybe she felt out of place at school

17:55.654 --> 17:59.407
because of me.

18:01.210 --> 18:04.208
That's in the past! I'll focus on now!

18:05.960 --> 18:14.093
Magical real physical
Magilulu nice bulk!

18:14.093 --> 18:16.929
Dreams are power!

18:16.929 --> 18:20.099
Dreams are power!

18:45.041 --> 18:47.835
Doing this every morning will kill me.

18:47.835 --> 18:51.672
Maybe I should've taken
the online course.

18:51.672 --> 18:55.343
But if I hadn't forced myself
to come up with a reason,

18:55.343 --> 18:57.537
I'd have been stuck like that forever.

18:58.304 --> 19:01.891
I'll have to walk,
but maybe I'll use another station.

19:02.600 --> 19:03.267
(Fairy Bouquet)

19:03.267 --> 19:05.227
(Fairy Bouquet)
The event's set, then.

19:05.227 --> 19:08.397
Lately, the manager's always angry.

19:08.397 --> 19:13.027
I'm apparently too slow at reposting
updates, or I make too many typos.

19:13.027 --> 19:15.096
No, that's just you being stupid.

19:15.613 --> 19:17.740
I know that!

19:17.740 --> 19:21.118
- Just copy and paste any proper nouns.
- Proper...?

19:21.869 --> 19:26.707
Ritsu, didn't your guitar stream
the other day hit 1000 live viewers?

19:26.707 --> 19:29.377
Wow! You just played the guitar?

19:29.377 --> 19:30.878
What else is there to do?

19:30.878 --> 19:35.633
If numbers are important,
the manager should let us do our thing.

19:35.633 --> 19:39.553
It's annoying that we can't stream
without permission.

19:39.553 --> 19:40.871
Ritsu.

19:41.513 --> 19:43.224
Say "ah."

19:43.224 --> 19:45.142
Ugh! How cute!

19:45.142 --> 19:46.769
Go ahead and eat it.

19:46.769 --> 19:50.356
Ritsu, you've been down since
bumping into Arale-chan.

19:50.356 --> 19:51.898
(Hot and cold duo on a date)
I just want you to cheer up.

19:51.898 --> 19:52.858
(Meme posted!)
I just want you to cheer up.

19:53.442 --> 19:58.989
I don't know what I'd do
without you, Ritsu.

20:01.617 --> 20:03.263
(Magical Physical Kululu Collab Café)
It was great.

20:03.263 --> 20:05.037
(Magical Physical Kululu Collab Café)
Yeah, it was awesome.

20:05.037 --> 20:06.747
(Magical Physical Kululu Collab Café)
So good.

20:07.289 --> 20:09.166
We're going to the bookstore.

20:09.166 --> 20:11.277
- Bye.
- See you.

20:18.039 --> 20:20.834
I guess I should be safe around here.

20:22.430 --> 20:24.432
(Akihabara Station)

20:47.321 --> 20:48.372
Small world!

20:48.372 --> 20:50.332
I'm sorry about yesterday.

20:50.332 --> 20:52.710
It's been so long, I was surprised.

20:52.710 --> 20:55.463
Your school's around here? Mine too!

20:55.463 --> 20:59.340
I'm not used to taking the train,
so rush hour is brutal.

20:59.340 --> 21:03.095
When someone pushes you,
you push the one in front of you.

21:03.095 --> 21:05.055
That's the sad reality of life.

21:05.055 --> 21:07.725
Akihabara's filled
with my favorite stores,

21:07.725 --> 21:09.727
so it's fun just to be here.

21:09.727 --> 21:12.271
I just went to a collab café.

21:12.271 --> 21:15.357
They give a sticker
for each item on the menu.

21:15.357 --> 21:17.609
That's such premium stuff!

21:17.609 --> 21:19.862
But I'm so full, I could explode.

21:19.862 --> 21:22.156
The place was tasty on its own,
so I recommend it.

21:22.156 --> 21:23.282
- The place was tasty on its own,
so I recommend it. - She's so loud.

21:23.282 --> 21:25.785
Hope it's sunny tomorrow! Bye!

21:28.234 --> 21:29.904
Is something going on?

21:34.928 --> 21:36.972
You're so out of reach now.

21:55.940 --> 22:03.781
Why can birds fly through the sky?
Why are cats always asleep?

22:03.781 --> 22:07.701
How will you live today?

22:07.701 --> 22:15.459
All, all, all of it
Let's go search for it all

22:19.672 --> 22:27.429
Why does the morning sun kiss my skin?
Why does the night leave me feeling down?

22:27.429 --> 22:35.729
If only we could split our sorrows in half
Wouldn't that be great?

22:35.729 --> 22:43.612
Laughter and worry interweave
In a corner of this vast world

22:43.612 --> 22:51.996
Come with us
To uncover the wonders of the universe

22:52.997 --> 23:00.880
What stories shall we share today?
What melodies shall we sing?

23:00.880 --> 23:04.717
Even flowers as yet unseen

23:04.717 --> 23:11.932
All, all, all of it
Let's go search for it all

23:12.641 --> 23:19.690
All, all, all of it
Let's go search for it all

23:25.905 --> 23:27.990
A band's impossible for me!

23:27.990 --> 23:29.241
No, it's not!

23:29.241 --> 23:31.869
- Manager-san...
- I know you can do this!

23:31.869 --> 23:36.582
You should be able to go all out!
Let's shout toward the sunset!

23:36.582 --> 23:39.710
Okay!
Next episode, "Smooch!"
